/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Reporting-Endpoints: csp-endpoint="https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report"
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://api.cireweddings.com https:; connect-src 'self' https://api.cireweddings.com; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; report-uri https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report; report-to csp-endpoint
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: img-src 'self' data: blob: https://api.cireweddings.com; report-uri https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report; report-to csp-endpoint

# Long-cache the immutable, content-hashed Astro bundles, the self-hosted font
# files (Schibsted Grotesk, Cormorant Garamond) included. Every path under
# /_astro/ carries a content hash in the filename, so a year-long cache is
# unconditionally safe: a changed file is a new URL, never the same one with
# different bytes.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The organiser portal is a STATIC Astro build on Cloudflare Pages, so the asset
# layer serves every response and this file covers all of them. (The guest site
# can't do that — it's an SSR Worker, which is why cire/invites carries its
# policy in `src/lib/security-headers.ts` middleware as well. Nothing here needs
# a middleware twin.)
#
# THIS FILE IS THE PRODUCTION POLICY. The build rewrites the copy in `dist/`
# (`src/lib/tier-headers.ts`): every `https://api.cireweddings.com` above
# becomes the origin of the `PUBLIC_CIRE_API_URL` the bundle was built with, so
# the dev tier allows and reports to its own API, and a local
# `wrangler pages dev dist` build allows the local one. Write only the
# production origin here; the build fails if this file stops naming it, or if
# the origin it writes appears in no client script.
#
# TWO POLICIES ON PURPOSE:
#
# 1. `Content-Security-Policy` is ENFORCED: the browser blocks whatever it does
#    not allow, and reports each block to the first-party collector
#    (`POST /api/csp-report` on cire-api — public, creds-less, 204-always). The
#    portal holds a session for the whole account and full guest lists, so it
#    must never be framed; `X-Frame-Options` above is the legacy twin of
#    `frame-ancestors`. Its `img-src` admits any `https:` image, for the shop
#    link picker (below).
#
# 2. `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` carries `img-src` WITHOUT `https:`,
#    plus the two reporting directives. It blocks nothing; it files a report
#    for every image the enforced policy loads only because of `https:` — the
#    picker's candidates, an avatar, or an image some injected markup points
#    off-site. Its `img-src` stays exactly the enforced one minus `https:`, and
#    it lists no other fetch directive: those are enforced and already report,
#    so repeating one here would file each violation twice. Dropping `https:`
#    from the enforced line means serving the picker's candidates through
#    cire-api first.
#
# Before changing either policy, walk the dev tier with its collector's logs
# open (`wiki/cire/cire-development.md`, "Portal security headers").
#
# WHY EACH SOURCE IS THERE (audited against the portal's source, not guessed):
#
#   script-src 'unsafe-inline'  Every built page carries three inline scripts:
#                               the theme-boot script (`THEME_BOOT_SCRIPT`, both
#                               page shells, `is:inline` so it runs before first
#                               paint), and Astro's own island loader and
#                               `astro-island` definition. The island chunks
#                               they load are `/_astro/*`, covered by 'self'.
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'   Astro inlines small critical CSS; Solid writes
#                               `style={{…}}` attributes (hence style-src-attr).
#   font-src 'self'             Schibsted Grotesk + Cormorant Garamond are
#                               SELF-HOSTED — `astro.config.mjs` downloads them
#                               at build time via `fontProviders.google()`. No
#                               fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com, unlike
#                               cire/invites, which still links the stylesheet.
#   img-src data: blob:         `data:` for the cropperjs canvas; `blob:` for
#                               it, for `lib/download.ts`'s object URLs and for
#                               the registry thumbnail `RegistryImageField`
#                               reads through `authFetch`.
#   img-src api.cireweddings…   Every uploaded image (invite art, event photos)
#                               is served by cire-api.
#   img-src https:              The registry's shop link picker
#                               (`RegistryImageField.tsx`) shows the candidate
#                               images `POST /registry/link-preview` returns
#                               straight from the shop's own host, which can be
#                               any https origin (cire-api emits `https:`
#                               candidates only). Enforced line only; the
#                               report-only line leaves it out on purpose.
#   img-src: avatars            The profile avatar comes from the OIDC `picture`
#                               claim and can name ANY https host, which
#                               `https:` admits; `ProfileMenu` renders only an
#                               https URL. OSN hosts no avatars yet, so nothing
#                               populates it. A set avatar loads and files a
#                               report-only report until its host is listed
#                               there: englishstventures/osn#1207.
#   connect-src                 cire-api only. Sign-in is a TOP-LEVEL redirect
#                               to musubi, not a fetch, and a navigation is not
#                               a connect-src subject — so the OSN origin is
#                               deliberately absent.
#   frame-src / worker-src      The portal embeds no iframes (Maps and Pinterest
#                               appear only as `href` links) and spawns no
#                               workers. 'none' both.
